Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:52:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Correct transformed point-sphere normals. Nonuniform object
 scale creates an ellipsoid, whose world-space normal requires the inverse
 transpose of its object-space normal.

Locked-Patch: patches/0003-point-nonuniform-normals.patch
Locked-Patch-SHA256: 3445bf84e54bfdd16e680a7d053a00b90f1f15a41e23c04e775bd71f1f3e784b
Contract: docs/renderer-patch-contracts.md
Related-Fixture: tests/houdini_points_smoke.py
Qualification: Source replay only; no new runtime qualification asserted.

Rebased-From: d1c9cddf32f619dfd79b838b24bbc2134b41e467
Previous-Patch: patches/0003-point-nonuniform-normals.patch
Previous-Patch-SHA256: 3445bf84e54bfdd16e680a7d053a00b90f1f15a41e23c04e775bd71f1f3e784b
Rationale: Nonuniform point transforms require inverse-transpose sphere normals; the geometry defect also affects non-Houdini consumers.
Contract: Correct transformed point-sphere normals. Nonuniform object scale creates an ellipsoid, whose world-space normal requires the inverse transpose of its object-space normal.
Tests: tests/houdini_points_smoke.py, scripts/verify-upstream-patches.py

diff --git a/src/kernel/geom/point_intersect.h b/src/kernel/geom/point_intersect.h
index 08704ca939eac7bb8000464e642d5bff3689970a..a05a06334dc1d7724e0e805e28214faf37c9739e 100644
--- a/src/kernel/geom/point_intersect.h
+++ b/src/kernel/geom/point_intersect.h
@@ -111,16 +111,19 @@ ccl_device_inline void point_shader_setup(KernelGlobals kg,
   float3 center = make_float3((isect->type & PRIMITIVE_MOTION) ?
                                   motion_point(kg, sd->object, sd->prim, sd->time) :
                                   kernel_data_fetch(points, position_offset + sd->prim));
-  if (!(sd->object_flag & SD_OBJECT_TRANSFORM_APPLIED)) {
-    object_position_transform(kg, sd, &center);
-  }
-
-  /* Normal */
 #  if defined(__GSPLATS__)
   if (isect->type & PRIMITIVE_POINT)
 #  endif
   {
-    sd->Ng = normalize(sd->P - center);
+    /* The ellipsoid normal is the inverse transpose of the object-space sphere normal. */
+    float3 P = sd->P;
+    if (!(sd->object_flag & SD_OBJECT_TRANSFORM_APPLIED)) {
+      object_inverse_position_transform(kg, sd, &P);
+    }
+    sd->Ng = normalize(P - center);
+    if (!(sd->object_flag & SD_OBJECT_TRANSFORM_APPLIED)) {
+      object_normal_transform(kg, sd, &sd->Ng);
+    }
   }
 #  if defined(__GSPLATS__)
   else {
